Vous avez dit :
what is reranking in rag

ChatGPT a dit :
Reranking in RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is the step where the system reorders retrieved documents or chunks to keep only the most relevant ones before sending them to the LLM.

Think of it as a second, smarter filter applied after retrieval and before generation.

Why reranking exists
Vector search is fast but imperfect:

It optimizes semantic similarity, not task relevance

It may return:

partially relevant chunks

redundant content

contextually wrong passages

Reranking fixes this by answering:

“Among these candidates, which ones best answer this question?”

Where reranking sits in a RAG pipeline
User query
   ↓
Embedding
   ↓
Vector search (top-K, e.g. 20)
   ↓
🔍 RERANKING (reduce to top-N, e.g. 5)
   ↓
Prompt construction
   ↓
LLM generation
What reranking actually does
Input
User query

List of retrieved chunks (documents, passages)

Output
Same chunks, reordered by relevance score

Often filtered (drop the weakest ones)

How reranking works (main approaches)
1. Cross-encoder reranking (most common)
A model evaluates query + document together.

Example:

Input:  [Query] + [Document chunk]
Output: relevance score
✔ Very accurate
❌ Slower (runs per document)

Typical models:

bge-reranker

cross-encoder/ms-marco

Cohere Rerank

OpenAI / Gemini rerank APIs

2. LLM-based reranking
An LLM judges relevance directly.

Example prompt:

“Rank these passages by how well they answer the question.”

✔ High quality
❌ Expensive
❌ Less deterministic

Used when:

High-stakes answers

Low latency not critical

3. Heuristic reranking (cheap, weaker)
Rule-based scoring:

keyword overlap

recency

document priority

metadata boosts

Often combined with ML rerankers.

Concrete example
User question

“What are the GDPR data retention rules?”

Vector search returns

GDPR overview (general)

Security best practices

Data retention article ✅

Consent management

Company privacy policy

Reranker output

Data retention article ✅

GDPR overview

Privacy policy

Consent management
❌ Security best practices dropped

Only top 2–3 go to the LLM.

Why reranking is critical
Without reranking:

hallucinations increase

answers become vague

irrelevant context pollutes prompts

token cost explodes

With reranking:

better answer quality

fewer tokens

higher factual grounding

more predictable behavior

Reranking vs retrieval (important distinction)
Step	Purpose
Retrieval	Find potentially relevant content fast
Reranking	Select actually relevant content accurately
In your architecture (ContextHub / RAG)
Reranking should:

Live inside ContextHub or RAG runtime

Be invisible to the Orchestrator

Be governed (which reranker, thresholds, limits)

The Orchestrator decides “RAG yes/no”,
ContextHub decides “which chunks exactly”.

One-sentence summary
Reranking is the step that turns “probably relevant” retrieved documents into “actually useful” context for the LLM.

